# Normalization rules applied to the staged tree before hashing and commit.
# Format: <path glob under the staging root><TAB><sed expression>
#
# Some backed-up files carry values that change on their own: Omarchy's theme
# rotation rewrites VS Code's colorTheme and dconf's icon theme on a timer,
# and themebook.json stamps a "last seen" time every few minutes. Left raw,
# these produce a stream of commits with no real change of intent, which is
# how a backup log stops being readable.
#
# The intent is still backed up (themebook favorites, default wallpapers, the
# cycle settings). Only the derived follower values below are neutralized,
# and Omarchy's own theme hook restores them on the next theme change.
#
# Add a newly discovered volatile field with one more line here, no code
# change needed. Keep expressions anchored and conservative: a bad sed rule
# can corrupt JSON, and normalize runs before every commit. Prefer deleting a
# line over inventing a placeholder value, since restore replays whatever is
# here and a placeholder must stay valid for the app that reads it.

home/.config/Code/User/settings.json	s/"workbench.colorTheme"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*"[^"]*"/"workbench.colorTheme": "Default Dark Modern"/g
# Delete, not placeholder: dconf.txt is fed to `dconf load` on restore, and a
# placeholder value would set a theme that does not exist. Omarchy's theme
# hook rewrites these anyway.
manifests/dconf.txt	/^icon-theme=/d
manifests/dconf.txt	/^gtk-theme=/d
manifests/dconf.txt	/^cursor-theme=/d
home/.config/omarchy/themebook.json	s/"lastAt": *[0-9][0-9]*/"lastAt":0/g
home/.config/omarchy/themebook.json	s/"wallpaperLastAt": *[0-9][0-9]*/"wallpaperLastAt":0/g
home/.config/omarchy/themebook.json	s/"lastSlug":"[^"]*"/"lastSlug":""/g
home/.config/omarchy/themebook.json	s/"lastPath":"[^"]*"/"lastPath":""/g
home/.config/omarchy/themebook.json	s/"recents":\[[^]]*\]/"recents":[]/g
